  "coverage_qualification": [
    "The target is an arbitrary Banach space. Continuous input ranges supply essential separability; separability of the whole target or dual is not assumed.",
    "The actual family and binary tensor universal properties give the independently specified canonical map. Its value is opaque. The omitted general item 1.1.3 is not resumed.",
    "One actual scalar test produces the normalized product kernel. The existing one-dimensional kernel, dilation and finite-coordinate Fubini retain every normalization and the zero-dimensional endpoint.",
    "The original finite Borel sums lie in the tensor image and approximate each smoothing in a common compact support step. Positive-parameter test convergence proves density in Federers literal final topology, without joint vector continuity or replacing it by the locally convex topology.",
    "Later items 4.1.4\u20134.1.34 remain required, including 4.1.33 and 4.1.34; pure historical remarks and external pointers are excluded by user scope."
  ],
